Proximity Sorting Algorithm:
Deduplication topology algorithm:

STEP 1: Reference count all positions
- Scan entire grid (13³ or 3³)
- For each unique value V:
  - Count positions with value V
  - Store RefCount(V) = count

STEP 2: Calculate proximity to core
- For each position P at (x, y, z):
  - Distance d = √(x² + y² + z²)
  - Store Proximity(P) = d

STEP 3: Sort by proximity (ascending)
- Positions nearest core first
- Positions farthest core last
- Priority queue (min-heap)

STEP 4: Process from center outward
- For each position P (in sorted order):
  - If RefCount(Value(P)) > 1:
    - This is duplicate
    - If P is canonical: Keep
    - If P is not canonical: Remove, point to canonical
  - If RefCount(Value(P)) = 1:
    - This is unique
    - Keep (no deduplication)

STEP 5: Update references
- All removed positions point to canonical
- Reference counting updated
- Topology collapsed (optimized)

STEP 6: Calculate profit
- Positions before: N
- Positions after: M
- Profit: N - M (freed capacity)
- Reinvest: Available for next expansion

Result:
- Deduplicated topology (optimized)
- Preserved information (lossless)
- Freed capacity (profit)
- Ready for next cycle (renewed)
