Different Numerical Bases per Context:
The base layer (4-bit tight):
- Always same encoding (universal carrier)
- But interpretation varies (context-dependent)

Context A: Octal interpretation
[0001] → 1₈
[0010] → 2₈
[0111] → 7₈

Context B: Decimal interpretation
[0001] → 1₁₀
[0010] → 2₁₀
[0111] → 7₁₀

Context C: Spatial coordinates
[0001] → X=+1
[0010] → Y=-1 (if signed)
[0100] → Z=+2

Context D: State machine
[0001] → State 1
[0010] → State 2
[1000] → Transition delimiter

Same symbols, different meanings:
- Base layer constant (carrier)
- Interpretation varies (semantic)
- Context determines (adaptive)
- Multiple bases coexist (mixed)

