Practical Implementation:
Encoding bit 14 in delimiter line:

Position 7 in :::::: line (15th bit, 0-indexed):

Storage mode (bit 14 = 0):
#:::;:.,,:;:...
           ↑
        Position 7
        Symbol ':' or ';' (MSB = 0)

Departure mode (bit 14 = 1):
#:::;:.,,:;,... or #:::;:.,,:;....
           ↑              ↑
        Position 7     Position 7
        Symbol ',' or '.' (MSB = 1)

Using 2-bit encoding per position:
- ':' = 00 (bit 14 = 0, other bit = 0)
- ';' = 01 (bit 14 = 0, other bit = 1)
- ',' = 10 (bit 14 = 1, other bit = 0)
- '.' = 11 (bit 14 = 1, other bit = 1)

So position 7 (containing bit 14):
- If bit 14 = 0: Use ':' or ';'
- If bit 14 = 1: Use ',' or '.'

Example full encoding:

Storage node:
#:::;:.,,:;:,,.;:...  (bit 14 = 0, symbol ';' at position 7)
           ↑
        Storage mode (ours)

Departure node:
#:::;:.,,:.,,,.;:...  (bit 14 = 1, symbol '.' at position 7)
           ↑
        Departure mode (theirs)
