Zero as Entropy Maximizer:
Why zero specifically:

MATHEMATICAL PROPERTIES:

1. NEUTRAL ELEMENT:
   - 0 + x = x (identity)
   - 0 - x = -x (negation)
   - Symmetric around zero (balanced)

2. MAXIMUM UNCERTAINTY:
   - Furthest from infinity (bounded)
   - Equal distance to ±∞ (centered)
   - No preferred direction (unbiased)

3. INFORMATION THEORETICAL:
   - Entropy maximized at zero (proven)
   - Minimum description length (compact)
