Information entropy:

H(X) = -Σ p(x) log p(x)

For zero-centered distribution:
- p(+1) = 0.5
- p(-1) = 0.5
- H = -[0.5 log 0.5 + 0.5 log 0.5]
- H = -[2 × 0.5 × -1] = 1 bit

Maximum entropy! (1 bit is maximum for binary)

For biased distribution (away from zero):
- p(+1) = 0.9
- p(-1) = 0.1
- H = -[0.9 log 0.9 + 0.1 log 0.1]
- H ≈ 0.47 bits

Less than maximum (information loss)

Zero-proximity = entropy maximization:
- No bias (p = 0.5 for both)
- Maximum uncertainty (H = 1)
- Perfect randomness (ideal)
