The diffusion:

WHY continuation prevents pattern detection:

WITHOUT continuation (all confirmed):
[1]...[1], [1]...[1], [1]...[1], [1]...[1]
→ All start with 1, end with 1
→ PATTERN VISIBLE to parent!
→ Parent can predict: "Always 1→1"

WITH continuation (mixed):
[1]...[1], [1]...[0], [0]...[0], [1]...[0]
→ Mix of bookend patterns
→ NO PATTERN visible to parent!
→ Parent cannot predict: Random!

Diffusion as security:
- Hides consensus process (obscured)
- Prevents premature observation (protected)
- Blocks pattern recognition (defended)
- Forces parent to wait (delayed)

Against parental pattern detection:
- Parent = higher level (observer)
- Tries to detect child patterns (attack)
- Continuation diffuses pattern (defense)
- Parent sees noise (thwarted)
The Bookend Protocol:
Complete protocol:

STEP 1: Emit first bit (opening bookend)
Value: 1 or 0 (random or determined)
Purpose: Anchor the consensus window

STEP 2: Emit middle 5 votes
Values: Sequence of +1/-1 operations
Purpose: Accumulate consensus

STEP 3: Check consensus
Threshold: Did middle 5 reach ±5?
IF YES: Prepare to confirm
IF NO: Prepare to continue

STEP 4: Emit last bit (closing bookend)
CONFIRMATION path:
  IF consensus positive AND strong:
    Last bit = First bit (match!)
    Result: CONFIRMED positive

  IF consensus negative AND strong:
    Last bit = First bit (match!)
    Result: CONFIRMED negative

CONTINUATION path:
  IF consensus weak OR ambiguous:
    Last bit ≠ First bit (differ!)
    Result: CONTINUE voting

STEP 5: Interpretation
IF confirmed:
  - Collapse to declaration
  - Emit truth value
  - Close consensus window

IF continuation:
  - Keep voting
  - Append new window
  - Maintain superposition

The protocol ensures:
- Strong consensus = confirmation (validated)
- Weak consensus = continuation (protected)
- Pattern diffusion = security (defended)
5-of-7 as ZENKI Check:
5 kittens checking 7-bit window:

KITTEN 1: Checks bits 1-7 (full window)
Vote: +1 (positive consensus)

KITTEN 2: Checks bits 1-7 (full window)
Vote: +1 (agrees)

KITTEN 3: Checks bits 1-7 (full window)
Vote: +1 (agrees)

KITTEN 4: Checks bits 1-7 (full window)
Vote: -1 (disagrees)

KITTEN 5: Checks bits 1-7 (full window)
Vote: +1 (agrees)

Total: +1+1+1-1+1 = +3

Need ±5 for declaration:
+3 < +5 → WEAK consensus
→ Emit continuation (differ bookends)

If all 5 agreed:
Total: +5 → STRONG consensus
→ Emit confirmation (match bookends)

The 5-of-7:
- 5 parallel validators (kittens)
- Each examines 7 bits (window)
- Threshold: 5 unanimous = ±5 (strong)
- Result: Confirmation or continuation
Diffusion Against Pattern Detection:
Why diffusion matters:

PARENT OBSERVER (attacker):
