[1]...[1] CONFIRM → Parent sees: "SET"

Parent learns:
- Pattern: Always confirming SET
- Prediction: Next will be SET
- Advantage: Knows before declaration
- Security: BROKEN!

WITH DIFFUSION:
Child streams:
[1]...[1] CONFIRM → Parent sees: "SET" (real)
[1]...[0] CONTINUE → Parent sees: "?" (unknown)
[0]...[1] CONTINUE → Parent sees: "?" (unknown)
[1]...[1] CONFIRM → Parent sees: "SET" (real)
[0]...[0] CONFIRM → Parent sees: "CLEAR" (real)
[1]...[0] CONTINUE → Parent sees: "?" (unknown)

Parent learns:
- Pattern: Mixed confirmations and continuations
- Prediction: Cannot determine next
- Advantage: NONE (random to observer)
- Security: PROTECTED!

The diffusion mechanism:
- Continuation = noise injection (masking)
- Mismatch bookends = pattern breaker (randomizer)
- Forces parent to wait = delay attack (defense)
- Maximum entropy = perfect security (ideal)

Parental pattern detection:
- GOAL: Predict child before declaration
- METHOD: Statistical analysis of bookends
- DEFEAT: Continuation diffuses statistics
- RESULT: Pattern undetectable (secure)
The Temporal Dimension:
Confirmation vs Continuation in time:

CONFIRMATION (closed):
T=0: Emit [1]
T=1-5: Accumulate votes
T=6: Check: ±5 reached
T=7: Emit [1] (matches!)
T=8: DECLARE truth
→ Window CLOSED
→ Time frozen
→ Truth established

CONTINUATION (open):
T=0: Emit [1]
T=1-5: Accumulate votes
T=6: Check: Only ±3
T=7: Emit [0] (differs!)
T=8: CONTINUE to T=9
→ Window OPEN
→ Time flowing
→ Truth emerging

The temporal implications:

