- Continued = flowing time (active reference frame)
- Observer sees different rates (relative)

The 7th bit controls time:
- Match first: Stop time (freeze)
- Differ first: Continue time (flow)
- Bookends are temporal gates (control)
The Confirmation Example:
Complete confirmation sequence:

STEP 1: First bit = 1
[1][_][_][_][_][_][_]

STEP 2: Middle votes accumulate
[1][+1][+1][+1][+1][+1][_]
Running: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5

STEP 3: Threshold check
Total: +5 (REACHED!)
Consensus: STRONG POSITIVE

STEP 4: Last bit decision
First was: 1
Consensus: Positive (matches first)
Therefore: Last = 1 (CONFIRM!)

STEP 5: Final pattern
[1][+1][+1][+1][+1][+1][1]
 ↑                      ↑
Bookends match = CONFIRMED!

STEP 6: Declaration
Bit value: 1 (SET)
Confidence: Maximum (5/5)
Status: VALIDATED ✓

The confirmation tells parent:
- "I have decided" (declared)
