The Continuation Example:
Complete continuation sequence:

STEP 1: First bit = 1
[1][_][_][_][_][_][_]

STEP 2: Middle votes accumulate
[1][+1][-1][+1][+1][-1][_]
Running: 1, 0, 1, 2, 1

STEP 3: Threshold check
Total: +1 (WEAK!)
Consensus: WEAK POSITIVE

STEP 4: Last bit decision
First was: 1
Consensus: Weak (questionable)
Therefore: Last = 0 (CONTINUE!)

STEP 5: Final pattern
[1][+1][-1][+1][+1][-1][0]
 ↑                      ↑
Bookends differ = CONTINUE!

STEP 6: No declaration
Bit value: UNDEFINED (still voting)
Confidence: Weak (only 3/5)
Status: CONTINUING...

STEP 7: Append new window
[0][_][_][_][_][_][_]
New first bit = previous last (0)
Continue accumulating...

The continuation tells parent:
- "Still voting" (undefined)
- "Consensus weak" (uncertain)
- "Truth emerging" (becoming)
- "Do not observe yet" (not ready)

Parent cannot exploit because:
- No pattern visible (diffused)
- Cannot predict (random to observer)
- Must wait for confirmation (forced delay)
- Security maintained (protected)
The 7-Bit Consensus Window:
Why 7 bits specifically:

7 = Prime number (indivisible)
7 = Harmonic root (÷7 in 1/7 = 142857)
7 = Days of week (temporal cycle)
7 = Notes in scale (musical harmony)
7 = ZENKI + 2 bookends (5 + 2)

The structure:

[Bookend 1][Vote][Vote][Vote][Vote][Vote][Bookend 2]
    ↑        └────────┬────────┘              ↑
  Anchor      5 consensus votes            Verify

BIT 1: Opening anchor (first bookend)
BITS 2-6: Consensus voting (5 votes)
BIT 7: Closing verify (last bookend)

Total: 7 bits (complete window)

The sacred 7:
- Beginning, middle, end (trinity)
- Opening, process, closing (cycle)
- Question, voting, answer (dialectic)
- 1 + 5 + 1 = 7 (balanced)

Like week:
- Sunday: Opening (first bit)
- Mon-Fri: Work week (5 votes)
- Saturday: Closing (last bit)
- Total: 7 days (cycle)

Like music:
- Do: Tonic (first bit)
- Re-Mi-Fa-Sol-La: Scale (5 notes)
- Ti: Leading tone (last bit)
- Total: 7 notes (octave minus one)

The 7-bit window IS:
- Complete cycle (temporal)
- Sacred structure (geometric)
- Consensus frame (logical)
- Truth container (semantic)
Implementation:
perl
sub consensus_7bit {
    my (@votes) = @_;  # Array of 7 bits

    die "Need exactly 7 bits" unless @votes == 7;

    my $first_bit = $votes[0];
    my $last_bit = $votes[6];
    my @middle_votes = @votes[1..5];

    # Calculate middle consensus
    my $consensus = 0;
    foreach my $vote (@middle_votes) {
        $consensus += ($vote ? +1 : -1);
    }

    # Check bookend relationship
    my $bookends_match = ($first_bit == $last_bit);

    if ($bookends_match) {
        # CONFIRMATION
        if (abs($consensus) >= 5) {
            # Strong consensus with matching bookends
            return {
                status => 'CONFIRMED',
                value => $first_bit,
                consensus_strength => abs($consensus),
                bookends => 'MATCHING',
                action => 'DECLARE'
            };
        } else {
            # Weak consensus but matching bookends
            # Unusual case - might be error
            return {
                status => 'WEAK_CONFIRM',
                value => $first_bit,
                consensus_strength => abs($consensus),
                bookends => 'MATCHING',
                action => 'REVIEW'
            };
        }
    } else {
        # CONTINUATION (diffusion)
        return {
            status => 'CONTINUATION',
            value => undef,  # No declaration yet
            consensus_strength => abs($consensus),
            bookends => 'DIFFERENT',
            action => 'CONTINUE_VOTING',
            diffusion => 'ACTIVE'  # Pattern detection defeated
        };
    }
}

# Example usage:
my @confirmed = (1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1);  # All ones
my $result1 = consensus_7bit(@confirmed);
# Result: CONFIRMED, value=1, DECLARE

my @continued = (1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0);  # Mixed with different bookends
my $result2 = consensus_7bit(@continued);
# Result: CONTINUATION, diffusion=ACTIVE
```

