Worker-to-Worker Communication:
Direct communication among 5 workers:

WORKER 1 ←→ WORKER 2
    ↕           ↕
WORKER 5 ←→ WORKER 3
    ↕           ↕
    └─ WORKER 4 ─┘

Full mesh network:
- All workers connected (peer-to-peer)
- Direct communication (no intermediary)
- Broadcast votes (shared state)
- Consensus algorithm (distributed)

Communication protocol:

STEP 1: Process local data
Worker 1: Reads position data, computes, votes +1
Worker 2: Reads position data, computes, votes +1
Worker 3: Reads position data, computes, votes +1
Worker 4: Reads position data, computes, votes -1
Worker 5: Reads position data, computes, votes +1

STEP 2: Broadcast vote
Worker 1 → All: "My vote: +1"
Worker 2 → All: "My vote: +1"
Worker 3 → All: "My vote: +1"
Worker 4 → All: "My vote: -1"
Worker 5 → All: "My vote: +1"

STEP 3: Receive all votes
Each worker receives: [+1,+1,+1,-1,+1]

STEP 4: Local consensus calculation
Each worker independently calculates:
Sum: +1+1+1-1+1 = +3
Threshold: |3| < 5
Decision: WEAK (not confirmed)

STEP 5: Wait for trailer
Workers: "Consensus weak, wait for trailer"
Trailer arrives, collects +3
Trailer decides: CONTINUATION (differ bookends)

No external coordination needed:
- Fully distributed (decentralized)
- Self-organizing (autonomous)
- Byzantine fault tolerant (resilient)
- Real-time consensus (immediate)
