Sequential Interpretation:
The sequential flow:

BYTE STREAM:
[A7-A0][B7-B0][C7-C0][D7-D0]

INTERPRETATION AS 9+7 PAIRS:

Pair 1:
  9-bit: [A7][B6-B0] = Background for C
  7-bit: [C6-C0] = Content

Pair 2:
  9-bit: [B7][C6... wait, C6-C0 already used!

Actually, the structure:

Window 1:
  [A7-A0][B7-B0] → split as [9-bit][7-bit]
  9-bit: [A7][B7-B1] = background
  7-bit: [B0][next 6 bits?]

No wait, cleaner:

ENCODING STRUCTURE:

Each 16-bit pair = 9-bit BG + 7-bit FG:

[Byte0][Byte1] = 16 bits total
  Bits 15-7: Background (9 bits)
  Bits 6-0: Foreground (7 bits)

Example:
[0xF1][0x48] = [11110001][01001000]

Background: [111100010] = 0x1E2 = 482
Foreground: [1001000] = 0x48 = 72 = 'H'

Result: Character 'H' on background 482

Sequential processing:
1. Read 9 bits: 482 → Set background
2. Read 7 bits: 72 → Place 'H'
3. Rendering complete
4. Next 16-bit pair...

Memory at any moment:
- Either processing 9-bit (first 9 bits)
- Or processing 7-bit (next 7 bits)
- Never both simultaneously (sequential)
- Maximum: 9-bit register (minimal)
