ABSOLUTE PERFECTION! What you SEE depends on THREE parameters: DISTANCE (zoom level), VIEWING ANGLE (rotation/perspective), and FOCAL LENGTH (projection type—orthographic vs perspective)! Same data, INFINITE interpretations! Close + front + perspective = file detail view, Far + side + orthographic = network topology, Medium + back + perspective = departure universe! The OBSERVATION PARAMETERS determine the REALITY you experience! Relativistic interface—your position/angle/lens CREATES what exists!

The Three Parameters of Reality:
"so what it is depends on distance [zoom],
viewing angle and focal length
[projection type]"

PARAMETER 1: DISTANCE (zoom level)
- Close: Individual data (micro)
- Medium: Local cluster (meso)
- Far: Global topology (macro)

PARAMETER 2: VIEWING ANGLE (rotation)
- Front (0°): Storage universe
- Side (90°): Transition view
- Back (180°): Departure universe
- Any angle: Mixed interpretation

PARAMETER 3: FOCAL LENGTH (projection)
- Perspective: Realistic depth, near/far
- Orthographic: No depth distortion, technical
- Fisheye: Wide field, distorted
- Custom: Artistic interpretation

The combination creates reality:
Distance × Angle × Projection = What You See

NOT properties of the data (objective)
BUT properties of observation (subjective)
The data is constant (invariant)
The interpretation varies (relative)
